      <h2 class="section-title section-title-glow">Amazon interview preparation — Leadership Principles are the system</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Map every behavioral story to a Leadership Principle.</strong> Amazon's 16 LPs are not background color — they are the evaluation framework. For every behavioral question, the interviewer is scoring you against specific LPs. Know all 16, understand what each means in practice, and map your best stories to 3–4 LPs each.</li>
        <li><strong>The STAR format is mandatory.</strong> Amazon behavioral interviews follow a strict structure: Situation, Task, Action, Result. Deviation from this structure is noticed. Practice until STAR is natural, not mechanical.</li>
        <li><strong>Bar Raisers look for culture, not just performance.</strong> The Bar Raiser's job is to evaluate whether you raise Amazon's overall bar — not just whether you can do this specific job. They will probe for LP alignment, especially on Ownership, Bias for Action, and Have Backbone/Disagree and Commit.</li>
        <li><strong>System design at Amazon scale.</strong> Amazon's infrastructure operates at a scale most engineers have never worked at. Design questions reflect this — be prepared to discuss distributed systems, event-driven architecture, and reliability patterns relevant to Amazon's actual systems (AWS, Prime, Alexa, fulfillment).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="content-panel">
      <h2 class="section-title section-title-glow">Microsoft and Seattle tech job search strategy</h2>
      <h3>Microsoft Interview Preparation</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Growth mindset stories are explicitly valued — prepare examples of learning from failure, updating your views based on evidence, and developing new skills outside your comfort zone</li>
        <li>Collaboration is evaluated specifically — stories where you influenced without authority, resolved conflict productively, and elevated colleagues are stronger at Microsoft than purely individual heroism stories</li>
        <li>Coding bar is high but slightly below Amazon's LP rigor for behavioral — the technical rounds are demanding, with medium-hard LeetCode and system design expected</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Seattle tech ecosystem beyond Amazon and Microsoft</h3>
